{
  "_provenance": {
    "captured": "2026-08-05",
    "why": "A Kalshi EVENT is a family of threshold strikes, and every event-level derivation must read all of them. kalshi_multi_close_event_2026_08_04.json pins close_time=max and is_resolved=all; this file pins the two derivations that moved off nested[0] on 2026-08-05 — the liquidity SUM and the withheld family price — at the point where each CHANGES A RENDERED CELL, which a fixture whose family sum lands in the same liquidity bucket as its first strike could not do.",
    "endpoints": {
      "kalshi": "https://api.elections.kalshi.com/trade-api/v2/events/{event_ticker}?with_nested_markets=true"
    },
    "edits": "Each event lifted verbatim from the free unauthenticated single-event endpoint; string values over 300 chars truncated. No key was renamed, added or removed, and no numeric value was touched — the sums the contract tests pin are hand-computed FROM these figures, so an edited number would silently move the expected value with it.",
    "events": {
      "KXGOVWINS-27JAN01": "3 all-active strikes whose family liquidity crosses a LABEL boundary: nested[0] alone is $3,387 volume / $3,130 OI (thin), the family sums to $107,079 / $31,470 (deep). The single clearest demonstration that the old read misreported the rendered `signal` column, and one of only 2 such 2-4-strike all-open events on the frozen universe. Also multi-strike, so `prob` must be withheld.",
      "KXNETANYAHUPARDON-26": "A COLLAPSED family: nested[0] is finalized and exactly one strike (index 1) is still active, so the price legs come from a strike that is NOT the first. A positional read here quotes the settled strike's realized $0.031 as a live price instead of the open strike's $0.175 midpoint. Its family liquidity EXCLUDES the settled strike's $16,234 of turnover ($3,791 rather than $20,026), which is the deliberate scope choice kalshi_tradeable_strikes documents: a settled strike publishes an empty book, so its midpoint is a synthetic $0.50 rather than a traded price."
    }
  },
